course: dictionary
lesson: 11785
title: Beholding: looking at something wonderful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Behold is an old word that means look or see. Beholding is its -ing form, so it describes someone who is looking at something. You will meet it in old stories, poems and carols. Read the words around it to find its meaning.
explain: «The children stopped, beholding the rainbow over the hills.» They did not just glance at it. The rainbow is wonderful, so beholding means looking at it in amazement. Check by swapping in another phrase: «The children stopped, looking at the rainbow in amazement» still makes sense.
explain: In the Bible, «Behold» means look! see! «Behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy.» The writer is telling you to pay attention, because something important is coming. The word is a signal that a wondrous sight or news is about to appear.
explain: The saying «Beauty is in the eye of the beholder» uses beholder, the person who sees. It means that different people can see beauty in different things. So the word often tells you that the sight matters.
fact: Behold means look or see, and beholding is its -ing form.
fact: «Beholding» means looking at something, especially something wonderful or surprising.
fact: In the Bible, «Behold!» means look! see!
fact: «Beholder» is in the saying «Beauty is in the eye of the beholder».
fact: Beholding is an old word, so you will mostly meet it in poems, carols and old stories.
exercise: «The children stopped, beholding the rainbow over the hills.» What does beholding mean here? | Hiding behind | Drawing a picture of | *Looking at, in wonder | Running away from
exercise: In the Bible, «Behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy» means what? | *Look! See! | Sleep now | Go away! | Be quiet
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to beholding? | Dropping | Forgetting | *Gazing at | Tasting
test: «Beholding the snowy mountains, Maya forgot about her cold feet.» Why did Maya forget her cold feet? | *The view was so wonderful she was lost in it | She had no shoes | She was angry at the mountains | She was asleep
test: In a carol, you read, «Behold the star above the stable!» What does behold mean? | Shout loudly | Hide from | Walk slowly past | *Look at this, see!
exam: «Beauty is in the eye of the beholder» means that the beholder is the one who | Is always right about everything | Closes their eyes to avoid seeing | *Sees and finds beauty in something | Owns the most beautiful things
